From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:22:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: don't drop a dynamic power reference NVPCF events
 never took

rm_acpi_nvpcf_notify() calls os_unref_dynamic_power() even when
os_ref_dynamic_power() failed, which has already undone its increment. The
refcount underflows, and the GPU can then be suspended while it is in use. Only
drop the reference after taking it.

Builds against 7.3; the failure path hasn't been run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/osapi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/osapi.c b/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/osapi.c
index cd44aba7..96c4eec8 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/osapi.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/osapi.c
@@ -6492,8 +6492,8 @@ void NV_API_CALL rm_acpi_nvpcf_notify(
             {
                gpuNotifySubDeviceEvent(pGpu, NV2080_NOTIFIERS_NVPCF_EVENTS,
                                        NULL, 0, 0, 0);
+               os_unref_dynamic_power(nv, NV_DYNAMIC_PM_FINE);
             }
-            os_unref_dynamic_power(nv, NV_DYNAMIC_PM_FINE);
         }
         rmapiLockRelease();
     }
